# Secrets for the Stripe TEST-mode deployment. Copy to `.test.vars`, which is
# gitignored (every `*.vars` is), fill it in, and push it with
#
#   node ../../scripts/push-worker-secrets.mjs .test.vars --env test
#
# `--env test` is not optional and the script now refuses without it. Wrangler
# applies secrets to the DEFAULT environment unless told otherwise, and the
# default here is the Worker taking real money at api.bastion.mgcrea.io — so the
# earlier version of this line replaced the LIVE webhook signing secret with a
# test-mode one. Every genuine payment was then refused as an invalid signature,
# and nothing said why until a buyer wrote in. The `test` environment is declared
# in wrangler.jsonc; deploy it once with `wrangler deploy --env test`.
#
# The same three keys as `.prod.vars`, from the test-mode side of the Stripe
# dashboard. The licence signing key is the SAME value as production: a key
# minted through a test purchase has to verify against the public key compiled
# into the app, or the end-to-end test proves nothing.
LICENSE_SIGNING_KEY=
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
